  "title": "The access lemma is a theorem: matching potentials are convex on a plane side",
  "subject": "Why a plane removed side composes: whether the removed line's hub always reaches the gluing ports when it pins them",
  "conclusion": "On a plane knot space minus a line, line-face matchings carry integer potentials forming an L-natural convex set whose parities are values relative to the hub, and rounded midpoints show that a hub pinning never selects a hub-tied port's state and otherwise points one step from the pinned pattern. So every pinned three-point knot through the hub is generated on a plane near side, whatever the far side.",
